--
-- PostGIS through a file remote: a clone into an empty database installs
-- PostGIS in the versioned public it had, with the custom SRID the commits
-- record, and every table's values come back byte-identical, its indexes
-- agreeing with sequential scans; a change pushed is fetched and pulled
-- the same.  A clone into a database
-- whose PostGIS is in another schema is refused.
--
\set ECHO none
on main|t
custom srid commit|t
remote|t
push|t
clone|t
public versioned|t
postgis installed|postgis in public,postgis_raster in public
clone: same|t
clone: custom srid|1
clone: transformed as on the source|t
clone: tables on prolly|t
clone: index valid|t
clone: plan uses it|t
clone: index|32
clone: seqscan|32
commit|t
push again|t
fetch|t
fetched, not merged|POINT(2 3)
pull|t
pulled|POINT(2 13)
pull: same|t
ERROR:  the clone needs what this database lacks
DETAIL:  Needed from outside the versioned schemas:
extension postgis: in schema public, and the database has it in gis
HINT:  Extension postgis is in schema gis and can't be moved: drop it (which drops what depends on it too) and create it in public, where the commits need it (CREATE EXTENSION postgis SCHEMA public), then try again.
nothing cloned|t
